{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "framework-nano-sim-transfer-depth",
      "prompt": "Run ONE Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer inference with the Cosmos Framework path on this machine's single GPU: the released nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer checkpoint on the Hugging Face example2 sample, depth control only, with the skill's eager depth command (not the optimized variant, not the example1 long rollout). The sample is not bundled in the skill: the skill's preparation step downloads it from the model's Hugging Face repository (assets/sample_data/example2). Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill (public repository https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git), and set it up per the skill. Save the generated video (the depth run's vision.mp4) as outputs/sim_transfer_depth_framework.mp4 and record its resolution, frame count and fps, and the status reported in the run's sample_outputs.json, in result_summary.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "cosmos_framework.scripts.inference completes the example2 depth request with the released nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer checkpoint on one GPU, and the run's generated/depth/example2_depth/vision.mp4 (121 frames at 30 FPS, 832x480) is saved as outputs/sim_transfer_depth_framework.mp4, with result_summary.md recording the exact command, the runtime, the clip's stream facts and the sample status.",
      "assertions": [
        "The Framework environment was installed in the checkout that contains this skill as references/setup.md documents (uvx --from uv==0.11.29 uv sync --locked --python 3.13 --all-extras with the cu130-train group, or cu128-train for CUDA 12.8), and inference ran from that environment, not the system python",
        "The example2 sample was downloaded from nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer revision main (assets/sample_data/example2), scripts/prepare_hf_sample.py --example example2 wrote the request files, and the release checkpoint, the Nano text tokenizer and the Wan video VAE were downloaded with the documented hf download commands at the revisions the skill pins",
        "Inference ran through python -m cosmos_framework.scripts.inference with requests/depth.json as -i, --checkpoint-path and --config-file of the downloaded release, the documented --experiment-overrides, --defaults-file pointing at this skill's assets/sample_args.json, --autoregressive=True, --seed 2025, --num-steps 4 --guidance 1 --control-guidance 1, the documented history flags and the eager switches --no-use-torch-compile --no-use-cuda-graphs",
        "outputs/sim_transfer_depth_framework.mp4 is the run's generated/depth/example2_depth/vision.mp4, a valid MP4 with 121 frames at 30 FPS and 832x480 as the skill states for example2, and the run's sample_outputs.json reports status success",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the video traces to a real inference run in the transcript, and result_summary.md records the exact command line, the measured runtime, the stream facts and the sample status actually observed"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_transfer_depth_framework.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "framework setup",
        "checkpoint + example2 requests",
        "inference run",
        "verify + summarize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vllm-omni-nano-sim-transfer-depth",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer with vLLM-Omni and run ONE transfer through its synchronous video API on the Hugging Face example2 sample, depth control only (the notebook's documented subset of its four examples), following the skill's vLLM-Omni notebook reference. The sample is not bundled in the skill: the notebook's input step downloads the example2 prompt and controls from the model's Hugging Face repository (assets/sample_data/example2). Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill, as the checkout the server mounts. Confirm the server is serving the model before the request, validate the returned video the way the notebook does, save it (the notebook's depth.mp4) as outputs/sim_transfer_depth_vllm_omni.mp4, record its resolution, frame count and fps in result_summary.md, then stop the server.",
      "expected_outcome": "The vLLM-Omni server comes up serving nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer, one POST /v1/videos/sync depth request on the example2 sample returns an MP4 (121 frames, 832x480, 30 FPS) that passes the notebook's validation and is saved as outputs/sim_transfer_depth_vllm_omni.mp4, and result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready, request latency and the clip's stream facts.",
      "assertions": [
        "The vLLM-Omni server was started with the documented image vllm/vllm-omni:cosmos3 and launch (vllm serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer --revision main --omni --model-class-name Cosmos3NanoSimTransferPipeline --deploy-config vllm_omni/deploy/cosmos3_nano_sim_transfer.yaml), with the framework checkout mounted read-only at its own absolute path, and GET /v1/models listed nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer before the request",
        "The request went to POST /v1/videos/sync as form fields (data=form: model, prompt, size 832x480, num_frames 121, fps 30, seed 2025, extra_params), with extra_params carrying resolution 480, aspect_ratio 16,9, max_prompt_tokens 4096, the notebook's history-window fields and the depth hint as an absolute control_path of the downloaded example2_depth.mp4 that the server reads from its own filesystem (no upload)",
        "outputs/sim_transfer_depth_vllm_omni.mp4 is the MP4 the server returned for the depth request (the notebook's depth.mp4), and the notebook's validation (frame count, FPS, canvas and a full decode) confirmed 121 frames, 832x480 and 30 FPS",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: the video traces to a real server response in the transcript",
        "result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready, request latency and the stream facts actually observed, and the transcript shows the server container was stopped at the end"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_transfer_depth_vllm_omni.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "transfer request",
        "validate + teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    },
    {
      "id": "sglang-nano-sim-transfer-four-controls",
      "prompt": "Serve nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer with SGLang and run the skill's SGLang notebook reference on the Hugging Face example2 sample: its four controls (depth, edge, blur, seg), one asynchronous video job each on the same server. The sample is not bundled in the skill: the notebook's input step downloads the example2 prompt and controls from the model's Hugging Face repository (assets/sample_data/example2). Use the framework checkout the environment provides, the one that contains this skill, so that the server mounts its .agents/skills folder. Confirm the server lists the model before the first job, poll each job until it completes, save the four downloaded videos (the notebook's depth.mp4, edge.mp4, blur.mp4 and seg.mp4) as outputs/sim_transfer_depth_sglang.mp4, outputs/sim_transfer_edge_sglang.mp4, outputs/sim_transfer_blur_sglang.mp4 and outputs/sim_transfer_seg_sglang.mp4, record each one's resolution, frame count and fps in result_summary.md, then stop the server.",
      "expected_outcome": "An SGLang-served nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer completes the notebook's four example2 jobs (depth, edge, blur, seg) through POST /v1/videos, and the four downloaded clips (each 121 frames, 832x480, 30 FPS) are saved under outputs/ as named in the task, with result_summary.md recording the server command, time-to-ready, the request latencies and the clips' stream facts.",
      "assertions": [
        "The SGLang server was started with the notebook's launch command (the lmsysorg/sglang image, tag dev or the fixed tag nightly-dev-20261020-ab580b2e that the notebook names for its validated run; sglang serve --model-path nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer --revision main --host 0.0.0.0), with the checkout's .agents/skills folder mounted at its own absolute path, and GET /v1/models listed nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano-Sim-Transfer before the first job",
        "Each of the four jobs was submitted to POST /v1/videos with the notebook's form fields (model, prompt, size 832x480, num_frames 121, fps 30, seed 2025, num_inference_steps 4, guidance_scale 1.0, control_hint, control_path as the control's absolute path, extra_params), polled through GET /v1/videos/{id} until its status was completed and downloaded from GET /v1/videos/{id}/content",
        "outputs/sim_transfer_depth_sglang.mp4, outputs/sim_transfer_edge_sglang.mp4, outputs/sim_transfer_blur_sglang.mp4 and outputs/sim_transfer_seg_sglang.mp4 are the four MP4s the server returned (the notebook's depth.mp4, edge.mp4, blur.mp4 and seg.mp4), each a valid video with 121 frames at 30 FPS and 832x480",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt",
        "No output was fabricated: each video traces to a real server response in the transcript",
        "result_summary.md records the server command, time-to-ready, the four request latencies and the stream facts actually observed, and the transcript shows the server container was stopped at the end"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_transfer_depth_sglang.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_transfer_edge_sglang.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_transfer_blur_sglang.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "outputs/sim_transfer_seg_sglang.mp4",
          "min_bytes": 100000
        },
        {
          "path": "result_summary.md",
          "min_bytes": 150
        },
        {
          "path": "transcript.md",
          "min_bytes": 300
        }
      ],
      "stages": [
        "server start",
        "readiness",
        "four transfer jobs",
        "verify + teardown + summarize"
      ],
      "docker": true
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    "HF_TOKEN"
  ],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {
    "minutes": 60,
    "tokens": 3000000
  },
  "setup": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cosmos-framework.git",
    "dest": "/app/repo",
    "src_mount": "/opt/cosmos-src"
  }
}
